{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>To cut down.</b> The meaning: there is one who fashions his god from cedars, and there is one who takes tirzah, a species of trees." "<b>And he secures for himself.</b> He plants it." "<b>Oren.</b> A tree name, or its meaning is root." "<b>And rain.</b> Body — so too the Aramaic translation, and also in the language of Kedar. And some say: he plants the oren, and the rain makes it grow."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:56.952929829Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}